menu "RadioFoundry Gateway common (common)"

    config RDOF_FEATURE_TX
        bool "Transmit-side burst work (regenerate, CSBK preambles)"
        default y
        help
            What a simplex or duplex MMDVM modem must be handed. The roamer's
            transmit path needs it; a receive-only build doesn't.

    config RDOF_FEATURE_DATA_BLOCKS
        bool "Data block decode (trellis 3/4, rate 1, CRC-9, CRC-32)"
        default y
        help
            Decoding data blocks and confirmed data. The call tracker doesn't need it
            (it counts blocks), so a receive-only gateway can leave it out.

    config RDOF_FEATURE_TRACKER
        bool "Call tracker and HBlink sink"
        default y
        help
            The call tracker: call start / end JSON, raw bursts and DMRD for what the radio hears.

    config RDOF_FEATURE_REPEATER
        bool "Duplex and single frequency repeater"
        depends on RDOF_FEATURE_TX
        default y

    config RDOF_RUST
        bool "rust's modules in place of their C files"
        depends on RDOF_FEATURE_TX && RDOF_FEATURE_DATA_BLOCKS && RDOF_FEATURE_TRACKER && RDOF_FEATURE_REPEATER
        default n
        help
            common ported to Rust a module at a time (rust/README.md lists them).
            The Rust is the build with every feature on, so it needs them all.
            Needs Espressif's Rust toolchain (espup install --targets esp32s3 --std).

endmenu
